mission "The Convoy That Never Arrived"
    name "The Convoy That Never Arrived"
    description "Investigate a merchant convoy whose ships vanished without a battle or wreckage."
    source "Isla Verde"
    destination "Santa Isabela"
    reward 1200
    speaker offer "Harbourmaster Rojas"
    speaker visit "Harbourmaster Rojas"
    speaker complete "Harbourmaster Rojas"
    to offer
        has "A Name Scratched in Brass: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Three merchant captains have filed reports about a convoy that never reached port. There was no distress signal, no wreckage, and no survivors to say which way the ships turned.`
            `Harbourmaster Rojas spreads the reports across the desk. "Ships do not simply vanish from a clear sea. Either someone took them, or someone made certain no one looked in the right place. I want the last known course checked against the expedition's records."`
            choice
                `"I will help you get to the bottom of it."`
                    accept
                `"Who else knows about this?"`
                    goto details
                `"I will leave this to a captain with fewer reservations."`
                    close
            label details
                `Rojas points to two entries in the harbour book. "The convoy's departure was entered, but its arrival was never written down. Find the discrepancy. If the same hand altered both records, we may finally have a name."`
                choice
                    `"I will take the risk. Put the destination on my chart."`
                        accept
                    `"I have other waters to cross. Good day."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Convoy That Never Arrived. Investigate a merchant convoy whose ships vanished without a battle or wreckage."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Santa Isabela, Rojas lays the convoy reports beside the older expedition papers. "No battle, no wreck, no account of the cargo," Rojas says. "That is not a lost convoy. That is a convoy someone wanted erased."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Rojas gathers the reports and ties them with cord. "I will keep copies in the harbour archive. If a governor asks for them, he can ask in front of the whole council. We are done letting one seal make a truth disappear."`
        log "Completed The Convoy That Never Arrived. Received 1200 gold. Investigate a merchant convoy whose ships vanished without a battle or wreckage."
